  "chapter": {
    "number": 23,
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 1,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "(Mizmor of Dovid)",
            "descriptive": true
          },
          {
            "text": "1Hashem is my Ro'eh (Shepherd);",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          },
          {
            "text": "I shall not lack.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 2,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "He maketh me to lie down in green pastures;",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          },
          {
            "text": "He leadeth me beside the mei menuchot (tranquil waters).",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 3,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "He restoreth my nefesh;",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          },
          {
            "text": "He guideth me in the paths of tzedek l'ma'an Shmo",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          },
          {
            "text": "(righteousness for the sake of His Name).",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 4,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Yea, though I walk through the Gey Tzalmavet (Valley of the Shadow of Death),",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          },
          {
            "text": "I will fear no rah (evil);",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          },
          {
            "text": "for Thou art with me;",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          },
          {
            "text": "Thy shevet (rod) and Thy staff they comfort me.",
            "poem": 1
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "line_break"
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 5,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Thou preparest a shulchan before me",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          },
          {
            "text": "in the presence of mine enemies:",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          },
          {
            "text": "Thou anointest my head with shemen (olive oil);",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          },
          {
            "text": "my kos runneth over.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 6,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Surely tov and chesed shall follow me",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          },
          {
            "text": "kol y'mei chaiyyai (all the days of my life):",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          },
          {
            "text": "and I will dwell in the Bais Hashem",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          },
          {
            "text": "l'orech yamim (for length of days, whole life long, forever).",
            "poem": 1
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
